  "executive_briefing": "The legislative advancement of the CLARITY Act through the U.S. Senate is actively establishing formal statutory guardrails, providing the legal certainty necessary to unlock alternative execution environments such as Bitcoin-native smart contracts. This regulatory harmonization coincides with an evolving institutional posture where spot Bitcoin adoption via ETFs has transitioned from initial launch euphoria into normalized macroeconomic portfolio integration. Consequently, the competitive landscape between Ethereum's dominant EVM architecture and Bitcoin's expanding utility is intensifying, supported by a structural shift toward trust-minimized, non-custodial cross-chain liquidity protocols that bypass vulnerable wrapped bridges.",
